        ("How do you explain conditional probability to a risk partner?", "P(A|B) is the share of B cases that are also A. The fraud rate among night transactions is not the share of fraud that happens at night. Those two conditionings are different.", "Swapping the condition and the event."),
        ("State Bayes' theorem in a fraud setting.", "P(fraud|alert) = P(alert|fraud) P(fraud) / P(alert). A precise alert on a rare event can still be mostly false alarms because P(fraud) is tiny.", "Equating the true positive rate with the probability the alert is a fraud."),
        ("What is a base-rate fallacy in a review queue?", "If fraud is 0.1% and the rule catches 80% of it while flagging 2% of legitimate transactions, most flags are still legitimate. Precision needs the base rate, not only sensitivity.", "Staffing a queue from recall alone."),
        ("When is a binomial model a reasonable fraud count model?", "When you have a fixed number of similar trials and a constant fraud probability, and the trials are close to independent. It is a poor model of a coordinated attack.", "Using a binomial test on clustered account-takeover events without comment."),
