        ("What is a broadcast join?", "The small table is copied to each executor so the large table does not move. It fails when the small table is not small.", "Broadcasting a fact table."),
        ("What is the difference between repartition and coalesce?", "Repartition can increase parallelism and usually shuffles. Coalesce reduces partitions without a full shuffle and is appropriate before a small write.", "Repartitioning down to one partition and shuffling the entire extract to do it."),
        ("How do you partition transaction files?", "By event date, so a training window reads a slice. Within a day, clustering by customer helps customer windows and hurts if every query filters a different key.", "A partition per customer, which creates a million tiny files."),
