        ("What is a shadow rollout in business language?", "We score and we do not change the customer outcome yet. We compare what we would have done with what we did, then we decide.", "A shadow period described as a launch."),
        ("How do you talk about a model failure?", "What broke, who was affected, what we did, what we changed, and what we still do not know. No narrative that protects the model.", "A postmortem that blames the data in the abstract."),
        ("What if the metric and the operation disagree?", "Believe the operation until you understand the gap. Offline precision that the queue does not see is a measurement bug, a latency bug, or a different population.", "Telling operations the dashboard is wrong because the notebook was higher."),
        ("How do you ask for a labeling budget?", "With the value of the decisions the labels would fix, the current blind spot, and the smallest sample that would change the model. Not with a request for more data in general.", "More labels, unspecified."),
